  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "The error occurred again, and this time we are able to reproduce it.  As ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "far as I can tell, it looks like when Fedora checks and verifies that a ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "foxml file is well-formed, it then creates a stub object, then checks ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "the datastreams.  If validation of the datastreams fails under certain ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "conditions, Fedora returns an error, but leaves the stub object in the ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "file system and in the database.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "To reproduce this:",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "The steps to reproduce the error are (using attached files)",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "1. Compare the content of DemoFail.xml and DemoSuccess.xml. They should ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "differ only in the location of the attribute xmlns:xlink: on the element",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "<foxml:digitalObject> (DemoFail) or <mods:mods> (DemoSucess).",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "2. Ingest object demo:failObject from DemoSuccess.xml; it should be ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "successful.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "3. Purge the object demo:failObject.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "3. Ingest object demo:failObject from DemoFail.xml; it will fail because ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "of the location of the xlink namespace declaration.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "4. Since the object was not ingested, try to repeat step 2. It will fail ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "with an ObjectAlreadyInLowlevelStorageException. At this point, you can ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "neither ingest nor purge the object demo:failObject.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
   "type": "doc",
