       "24x24": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/8e627ad1f07d2a95bfd257d6c78c26a6?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FAB-6.png",
       "32x32": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/8e627ad1f07d2a95bfd257d6c78c26a6?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FAB-6.png",
       "48x48": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/8e627ad1f07d2a95bfd257d6c78c26a6?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FAB-6.png"
      },
      "displayName": "Aaron Birkland",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=5ed02cb2dacd410c1f9e56ae",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": "<p>Fixed the obvious un-recoverability problem by removing unnecessary retrievals from storage, instead relying on already known/retrieved/submitted data.   Added a validating deserialization step to discover errors in a controlled fashion and provoke a failure upon ingest.  The changes end up balancing out as far as performance, with the submitted fix perhaps achieving a very slight performance increase</p>\n\n<p>Used a live system test to verify fix, in configB only.  DOManager itself is a bit too unweildy to test with an offline test without a significant amount of effort.</p>\n",
     "created": "25/Nov/09 4:20 PM",
     "id": "11114",
     "jsdPublic": true,
     "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/issue/10527/comment/11114",
